            <ArticleTitle>[Sleep and nocturnal incontinence in hospital or institutional care].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1268-6034(17)30100-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.sger.2017.05.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A survey carried out in 2004 studied the link between quality of sleep and the nocturnal management of incontinence. This same survey was repeated 10 years later. The results reveal the impact on quality of sleep, the deteriorating management of incontinence with the lenghtening of waiting time and the causes of waking. This discussion process on the quality of sleep must continue.</AbstractText>
